# Extra protected path prefixes for THIS project. One per line; `#` comments
# and blank lines are ignored. Read by the path guards of all four hosts
# (.claude/hooks/protect-paths.sh and the .codex/.gemini protect_paths.py
# siblings), so a rule added here holds whichever agent is working.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS ONLY ON THE TEMPLATE (T-00000031). `.agents/bin/` is
# vendored kit code: in YOUR project nobody should edit it locally, because the
# next kit upgrade overwrites it and your change is lost silently. In the kit's
# own repository the opposite is true — that directory is where the kit
# maintains itself — so the file is declared `own:` in `.template-exclude` and
# never travels back to main.
#
# To let an agent touch a protected path anyway: remove or comment the line
# here, or ask for explicit approval. Never work around the hook.

.agents/bin/
